# Pinned third-party FFmpeg builds used by Shrinkr — the release workflow
# sidecars (release.yml) and the in-app Windows download (core/src/ffmpeg_fetch.rs)
# verify every download against this file before anything is unpacked or run.
# Verify locally with: sha256sum -c FFMPEG-PINS.sha256
#
# Bump procedure (see FFMPEG-NOTES.txt for attribution/licensing):
#   1. Pick the new artifact (FFmpeg-Builds: use a dated `autobuild-YYYY-MM-DD`
#      release tag, whose asset names are immutable — never the floating
#      "latest" tag, whose assets are replaced on rebuilds).
#   2. Download it, run it through the release sanity check, then add the
#      asset name + SHA-256 here and update the URLs in release.yml and
#      ffmpeg_fetch.rs to the same pinned tag.
#   3. Record the build in FFMPEG-NOTES.txt.
# Windows x64 — FFmpeg-Builds master autobuild N-128889-g88c46fce27 (2026-11-13)
# https://github.com/FFmpeg-Builds/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/autobuild-2026-11-13-12-43/ffmpeg-N-128889-g88c46fce27-win64-gpl.zip
35fa1c17eeead1f572072b134458788caf71c4a7fbce9e0bb2f3c41032959531  ffmpeg-N-128889-g88c46fce27-win64-gpl.zip
# Linux x64 — same build as the Windows pin
# https://github.com/FFmpeg-Builds/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/autobuild-2026-11-13-12-43/ffmpeg-N-128889-g88c46fce27-linux64-gpl.tar.xz
efa8f93583e84d5a1036e7e08e19db9f03ca637d7620ed58b0ecca39e9e34323  ffmpeg-N-128889-g88c46fce27-linux64-gpl.tar.xz
